WEBVTT

00:00:02.979 --> 00:00:03.715
Dad wants us to pick up
where he left off --

00:00:04.818 --> 00:00:07.794
Saving people, hunting things,
the family business.

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:13.115
You know the truth
about sammy.

00:00:13.148 --> 00:00:15.656
I've known for a while.

00:00:15.689 --> 00:00:18.865
You get premonitions
of people about to die?

00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:20.971
Death visions?

00:00:21.005 --> 00:00:22.174
Yeah.

00:00:22.209 --> 00:00:24.650
Sam: the demon
said he had plans for me.

00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:27.156
Do you have any idea
what he meant by that?

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:28.861
No.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:31.903
I want you to watch out
for sammy, okay?

00:00:31.936 --> 00:00:34.244
Did he say anything
to you?

00:00:34.277 --> 00:00:36.250
No.

00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:39.125
I can't talk about this
to sammy.

00:00:39.159 --> 00:00:41.131
I've got to keep
my game face on.

00:00:41.165 --> 00:00:43.807
You're erratic,
except for when you're hunting.

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:45.611
'Cause then,
you're downright scary.

00:00:46.648 --> 00:00:48.954
The truth is,
i'm not handling it very well.

00:00:49.457 --> 00:00:54.136
You're tailspinning, man,
and you won't let me help you.

00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:25.798
No, no, no, no.
No, you're not gonna --

00:01:25.832 --> 00:01:28.472
No, i swear!
It's not in me!

00:01:28.506 --> 00:01:31.012
Oh, god.
We're all gonna die.

00:01:31.046 --> 00:01:32.484
Maybe he's telling
the truth.

00:01:32.518 --> 00:01:34.423
He's not him --
Not anymore.

00:01:34.456 --> 00:01:37.164
Stop it! Ask her!
Ask the doctor!

00:01:37.197 --> 00:01:38.669
It's not in me!

00:01:38.703 --> 00:01:40.274
I...just...

00:01:41.477 --> 00:01:42.848
i can't tell.

00:01:42.882 --> 00:01:45.322
No, please, don't.
Don't.

00:01:45.356 --> 00:01:48.063
I've got no choice.

00:01:48.097 --> 00:01:50.705
It's not in me.

00:02:12.201 --> 00:02:13.472
Sam?

00:02:16.493 --> 00:02:20.251
<Font color="#ffff00">www.1000fr.Com present</font>

00:02:20.251 --> 00:02:25.229
uploaded for opensubtitles.org by najic (",)

00:02:28.559 --> 00:02:31.290
<i>Woman:
continue on or-224 west.</i>

00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:33.800
There are only two towns
in the u.S. Named rivergrove.

00:02:33.833 --> 00:02:36.508
How come you're so sure
it's the one in oregon?

00:02:37.845 --> 00:02:40.954
There was a picture.

00:02:43.027 --> 00:02:44.665
Okay, what else?

00:02:44.699 --> 00:02:49.880
I saw a dark room, some people,
and a guy tied to a chair.

00:02:49.915 --> 00:02:51.720
And i ventilated him?

00:02:51.753 --> 00:02:55.464
Yeah. You thought there was
something inside him.

00:02:55.497 --> 00:02:59.039
A demon? Was he possessed?

00:02:59.039 --> 00:02:59.375
All your weirdo visions

00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:01.247
Are always tied to
the yellow-Eyed demon.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.057
Was there any black smoke?
Did we try to exorcise him?

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.998
No. Nothing.
You just plugged him.

00:03:07.031 --> 00:03:08.001
That's it.

00:03:08.034 --> 00:03:09.774
Well, i'm sure
i had a good reason.

00:03:09.807 --> 00:03:11.780
I sure hope so.

00:03:14.072 --> 00:03:16.847
What does that mean?

00:03:18.083 --> 00:03:21.327
I'm not gonna
waste an innocent man.

00:03:21.626 --> 00:03:23.230
I wouldn't.
I never said you would.

00:03:23.264 --> 00:03:24.668
Fine.
Fine.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.306
Look, we don't
know what it is.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:29.015
But whatever it is, that guy
in the chair is a part of it.

00:03:29.047 --> 00:03:31.021
So, let's find him
and see what's what.

00:03:31.086 --> 00:03:32.624
Fine.
Fine.

00:04:16.388 --> 00:04:17.726
He was there.

00:04:21.503 --> 00:04:22.473
Morning.

00:04:22.506 --> 00:04:24.779
Morning.
Can i help you?

00:04:24.814 --> 00:04:27.688
Yeah. Billy gibbons,
frank beard.

00:04:27.722 --> 00:04:29.126
U.S. Marshals.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.998
What's this about?

00:04:31.032 --> 00:04:32.035
We're looking for someone.

00:04:32.068 --> 00:04:34.876
A young man, early 20s.

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:39.758
He'd have a thin scar
right below his hairline.

00:04:39.791 --> 00:04:41.697
What did he do?

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.301
We're actually
looking for someone else,

00:04:43.335 --> 00:04:45.474
But we think
this young man can help us.

00:04:45.508 --> 00:04:48.183
He's not in any kind of trouble
or anything. Not yet.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.604
I think maybe you
know who he is, master sergeant.

00:04:55.638 --> 00:04:58.781
My dad was in the corps.
He was a corporal.

00:04:58.815 --> 00:04:59.784
What company?

00:04:59.818 --> 00:05:01.122
Echo-2-1.

00:05:01.155 --> 00:05:02.559
So, can you help us?

00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:09.313
Duane tanner's
got a scar like that.

00:05:09.345 --> 00:05:11.084
But i know him.

00:05:11.117 --> 00:05:13.123
Good kid.
Keeps his nose clean.

00:05:13.157 --> 00:05:15.999
Oh, i'm sure he does.
Do you know where he lives?

00:05:16.032 --> 00:05:21.181
With his family,
up aspen way.

00:05:21.214 --> 00:05:22.184
Thank you.

00:05:22.217 --> 00:05:24.223
Thanks.

00:05:36.393 --> 00:05:38.265
Hey.

00:05:46.055 --> 00:05:47.458
"Croatoan"?

00:05:47.491 --> 00:05:48.595
Yeah.

00:05:49.732 --> 00:05:52.808
Roanoke. Lost colony.
Ring a bell?

00:05:52.841 --> 00:05:56.151
Dean, did you pay any attention
to history class?

00:05:56.185 --> 00:05:59.127
Yeah. The shot heard
around the world.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.832
How bills become laws.

00:06:00.865 --> 00:06:04.275
That's not school.
That's "schoolhouse rock."

00:06:05.712 --> 00:06:06.682
Whatever.

00:06:06.715 --> 00:06:08.654
Roanoke was one
of the first

00:06:08.688 --> 00:06:11.397
English colonies in america --
Late 1500s.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.436
Oh, yeah, yeah,
i do remember that.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.275
The only thing
they left behind

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:17.782
Was a single word carved
in a tree.

00:06:17.815 --> 00:06:19.053
"Croatoan."

00:06:19.086 --> 00:06:21.025
Yeah, and there were
theories --

00:06:21.059 --> 00:06:22.128
Indian raid, disease --

00:06:22.162 --> 00:06:23.733
But nobody knows
what really happened.

00:06:23.766 --> 00:06:27.411
They were all just gone,
wiped out overnight.

00:06:27.445 --> 00:06:31.356
You don't think
that's what's going on here.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.830
Whatever i saw in my head,
it sure wasn't good.

00:06:36.304 --> 00:06:37.942
But what do you think
could do that?

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:44.462
Well, i mean, like i said,
all your weirdo visions

00:06:44.496 --> 00:06:47.471
Are always tied to the
yellow-Eyed demon somehow, so...

00:06:47.505 --> 00:06:50.146
we should get help.

00:06:50.179 --> 00:06:52.385
Bobby. Ellen, maybe.

00:06:52.418 --> 00:06:54.458
Yeah,
that's a good idea.

00:06:59.473 --> 00:07:01.647
I don't have a signal.

00:07:07.497 --> 00:07:09.671
I don't either.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:23.110
The line's dead.

00:07:23.143 --> 00:07:24.780
I'll tell you one thing --

00:07:24.815 --> 00:07:26.687
If i was gonna
massacre a town,

00:07:26.721 --> 00:07:29.328
That'd be my first step.

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:48.720
Yeah?

00:07:48.753 --> 00:07:51.293
Hi, looking for duane tanner.
He lives here, right?

00:07:51.327 --> 00:07:53.567
He's my brother.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.172
Can we talk to him?

00:07:55.205 --> 00:07:57.278
He's not here right now.

00:07:57.311 --> 00:07:58.515
Do you know where he is?

00:07:58.549 --> 00:08:01.725
Yeah, he went on a fishing trip
up by roslyn lake.

00:08:01.758 --> 00:08:03.564
Your parents home?
Yeah, they're inside.

00:08:03.597 --> 00:08:04.600
Man:
jake, who is it?

00:08:06.238 --> 00:08:08.879
Dean:
hi, u.S. Marshals, sir.

00:08:08.912 --> 00:08:11.553
We're looking
for your son duane.

00:08:11.588 --> 00:08:12.890
He's not in trouble,
is he?

00:08:12.924 --> 00:08:15.565
We just need to ask him
a couple routine questions.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.739
When is he due back
from his trip?

00:08:17.773 --> 00:08:19.310
I'm not sure.

00:08:19.344 --> 00:08:22.520
Well,
maybe your wife knows.

00:08:22.553 --> 00:08:25.027
No, i don't know.
She's not here right now.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.432
Well,
your son said she was.

00:08:26.465 --> 00:08:27.501
Did i?

00:08:27.535 --> 00:08:30.309
She's getting groceries.

00:08:30.342 --> 00:08:32.215
So, when duane gets back,

00:08:32.248 --> 00:08:34.456
There's a number
where he can get ahold of you?

00:08:34.489 --> 00:08:36.796
Oh, no, we'll just check in
with you later.

00:08:42.212 --> 00:08:44.686
That was kind of creepy,
right?

00:08:44.719 --> 00:08:46.022
A little too stepford?

00:08:46.056 --> 00:08:47.896
Big-Time.

00:08:58.192 --> 00:09:02.539
It's okay, mom.
It's not gonna hurt.

00:09:22.832 --> 00:09:24.270
Put it down!

00:10:02.329 --> 00:10:04.803
Hello?

00:10:04.836 --> 00:10:07.176
Hello?
We need a doctor here.

00:10:08.843 --> 00:10:10.649
Mrs. Tanner,
what happened?

00:10:10.683 --> 00:10:11.819
She's been attacked.

00:10:11.852 --> 00:10:12.855
Dr. Lee?

00:10:15.964 --> 00:10:16.934
It's okay.

00:10:16.967 --> 00:10:18.673
Bring her in.

00:10:18.706 --> 00:10:19.876
Okay.

00:10:21.815 --> 00:10:23.788
Hey.

00:10:23.821 --> 00:10:26.497
Is that...?

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.305
Mr. Tanner?

00:10:29.338 --> 00:10:31.311
Was he attacked, too?

00:10:31.344 --> 00:10:33.618
Uh, no, actually,
he did the attacking,

00:10:33.651 --> 00:10:35.456
And then
he got himself shot.

00:10:35.489 --> 00:10:36.826
Shot?
Yeah.

00:10:36.859 --> 00:10:38.064
And who are you?

00:10:38.097 --> 00:10:41.239
U.S. Marshal.
I'd show you my badge, but...

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:43.880
oh, sorry.
Bring him back here.

00:10:46.054 --> 00:10:48.194
Wait, you said jake
helped him?

00:10:48.227 --> 00:10:50.033
Your son jake?

00:10:50.066 --> 00:10:52.272
They beat me.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:55.950
Tied me up.

00:10:55.983 --> 00:10:58.925
I don't believe it.

00:10:58.959 --> 00:11:00.263
Pam.

00:11:00.296 --> 00:11:02.436
Beverly,
do you have any idea

00:11:02.469 --> 00:11:04.040
Why they would act
this way?

00:11:04.074 --> 00:11:05.980
Any history
of chemical dependency?

00:11:06.013 --> 00:11:08.320
No, of course not.

00:11:08.354 --> 00:11:10.293
I don't know why.

00:11:10.326 --> 00:11:15.007
One minute,
they were my husband and my son,

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.387
And the next,
they had the devil in them.

00:11:22.094 --> 00:11:23.934
We've got to talk.

00:11:30.252 --> 00:11:32.291
Those guys were whacked
out of their gourds.

00:11:32.325 --> 00:11:34.197
What do you think,
mass possession?

00:11:34.231 --> 00:11:36.705
If it is a possession,
there could be more.

00:11:36.738 --> 00:11:37.876
God knows how many.

00:11:37.909 --> 00:11:39.982
It could be like
a freaking shriner convention.

00:11:40.014 --> 00:11:43.924
Of course, that's one way
to wipe out a town --

00:11:43.924 --> 00:11:44.629
You take it
from the inside.

00:11:44.662 --> 00:11:47.303
We didn't see any
of the demon smoke with tanner

00:11:47.336 --> 00:11:48.859
Or any
of the other usual signs.

00:11:48.859 --> 00:11:52.183
Something turned him
into a monster.

00:11:52.217 --> 00:11:55.133
You know, if you would have
taken out the other one,

00:11:55.133 --> 00:11:56.725
There would be one less
to worry about.

00:11:56.725 --> 00:11:58.918
I'm sorry.
I hesitated.

00:11:58.919 --> 00:11:59.989
It was a kid.

00:12:00.024 --> 00:12:01.259
No, it was an "it."

00:12:01.292 --> 00:12:04.904
It's not the best time
for a bleeding heart, sam.

00:12:04.937 --> 00:12:06.241
How's the patient?

00:12:06.274 --> 00:12:08.247
Terrible. What the hell
happened out there?

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.253
You just killed
my next-Door neighbor.

00:12:10.286 --> 00:12:11.423
We didn't have a choice.

00:12:11.457 --> 00:12:14.348
Maybe so,
but we need the county sheriff.

00:12:14.348 --> 00:12:15.192
The phones are down.

00:12:15.192 --> 00:12:17.733
I know. I tried. Tell me
you've got a police radio.

00:12:17.766 --> 00:12:20.709
Yeah, we do, but it crapped out
just like everything else.

00:12:20.742 --> 00:12:22.748
I don't understand
what is happening.

00:12:22.781 --> 00:12:23.919
How far is it
to the next town?

00:12:23.952 --> 00:12:25.890
It's about 40 miles down
to sidewinder.

00:12:25.925 --> 00:12:28.162
I'm gonna go down there
and see if i can find some help.

00:12:28.163 --> 00:12:30.972
My partner will stick around
and keep you guys safe.

00:12:31.005 --> 00:12:32.743
Safe from what?

00:12:34.816 --> 00:12:37.157
We'll get back to you
on that.

00:13:58.999 --> 00:14:01.340
Huh.

00:14:03.446 --> 00:14:04.584
What?

00:14:04.617 --> 00:14:07.758
His lymphocyte percentage
is pretty high.

00:14:07.792 --> 00:14:10.434
His body was fighting off
a viral infection.

00:14:10.467 --> 00:14:13.041
Really?
What kind of virus?

00:14:13.075 --> 00:14:14.813
I can't say for sure.

00:14:14.846 --> 00:14:17.336
An infection could have made him
act like that?

00:14:17.337 --> 00:14:21.921
Some can cause dementia,
but not that kind of violence.

00:14:21.921 --> 00:14:23.259
And besides,

00:14:23.259 --> 00:14:25.243
I've never heard of one
that did this to the blood.

00:14:25.243 --> 00:14:26.166
Did what?

00:14:26.166 --> 00:14:28.018
There's
this weird residue.

00:14:28.907 --> 00:14:32.283
If i didn't know better,
i'd say it was sulfur.

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:40.542
Sulfur.

00:15:14.542 --> 00:15:16.282
Oh, ho, ho. Hey.

00:15:16.315 --> 00:15:17.953
Sorry. Road's closed.

00:15:17.986 --> 00:15:20.126
Yeah, i can see that.
What's up?

00:15:20.159 --> 00:15:21.297
Quarantine.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:23.636
Quarantine?
What is it?

00:15:23.670 --> 00:15:24.974
Don't know.

00:15:25.007 --> 00:15:26.812
Something going around
out there.

00:15:26.845 --> 00:15:28.651
Uh-Huh.
Who told you that?

00:15:28.685 --> 00:15:29.989
County sheriff.

00:15:30.022 --> 00:15:31.459
Is he here?

00:15:31.492 --> 00:15:33.900
No. He called.

00:15:33.933 --> 00:15:35.604
Say, why don't
you get out of the car,

00:15:35.638 --> 00:15:37.009
And we'll talk a little?

00:15:37.043 --> 00:15:39.417
Well,
you are a handsome devil,

00:15:39.451 --> 00:15:41.991
But i don't swing that way,
sorry.

00:15:42.024 --> 00:15:44.231
I'd sure appreciate it
if you got out of the car,

00:15:44.264 --> 00:15:45.368
Just for a quick minute.

00:15:47.507 --> 00:15:49.646
Yeah, i bet you would.

00:15:51.719 --> 00:15:53.525
Stop!

00:15:53.558 --> 00:15:54.661
Stop!

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.211
I don't understand.

00:16:11.244 --> 00:16:15.558
Are you saying my husband
and jake had a disease?

00:16:15.623 --> 00:16:17.797
That's what
we're trying to find out.

00:16:17.831 --> 00:16:21.809
Now, during the attack,
do you remember --

00:16:21.843 --> 00:16:25.687
Did you have any direct contact
with their blood?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:26.958
Oh, my god.

00:16:26.991 --> 00:16:30.335
You don't think
i've got this virus, do you?

00:16:30.368 --> 00:16:32.808
Beverly, i don't know
what to think,

00:16:32.841 --> 00:16:36.185
But with your permission,
we'll take a blood sample.

00:16:46.081 --> 00:16:47.185
Aah!

00:16:47.953 --> 00:16:49.090
Aah!

00:16:54.272 --> 00:16:55.610
Aah!

00:17:08.248 --> 00:17:09.552
Hands where
i can see them!

00:17:09.585 --> 00:17:10.887
Son of a --

00:17:10.922 --> 00:17:12.793
Get out of the car!

00:17:14.164 --> 00:17:15.369
Out of the car!

00:17:15.402 --> 00:17:17.875
Crap.

00:17:17.908 --> 00:17:19.982
All right.
Easy there, big guy.

00:17:23.993 --> 00:17:25.298
Put it down!
Lower it now!

00:17:25.331 --> 00:17:26.301
Are you one of them?!

00:17:26.334 --> 00:17:27.304
No, are you?!
No!

00:17:27.337 --> 00:17:29.811
You could be lying!
So could you!

00:17:29.844 --> 00:17:31.950
We could do this all day.
All right.

00:17:31.984 --> 00:17:34.759
Let's just take it easy
before we kill each other.

00:17:36.932 --> 00:17:38.905
What's going on
with everybody?

00:17:38.938 --> 00:17:40.911
I don't know.

00:17:40.944 --> 00:17:43.017
My neighbor, mr. Rogers --

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:45.023
You've got a neighbor
named mr. Rogers?

00:17:45.056 --> 00:17:46.260
Not anymore.

00:17:46.294 --> 00:17:50.272
He came at me with a hatchet.
I put him down.

00:17:50.306 --> 00:17:51.777
He's not the only one.

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:54.217
I mean, it's happening
to everyone.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:55.388
I'm heading to doc's place.

00:17:55.421 --> 00:17:56.891
There's still
some people left.

00:17:56.924 --> 00:17:58.095
I'm getting the hell out.

00:17:58.129 --> 00:18:00.268
There's no way out.
They got the bridge covered.

00:18:00.301 --> 00:18:02.743
I don't believe you.
Fine, stay here.
Be my guest.

00:18:19.325 --> 00:18:22.166
Well, this ought to be
a relaxing drive.

00:18:28.552 --> 00:18:31.227
What if we all have it?

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:34.069
What if we all go crazy?

00:18:34.102 --> 00:18:36.208
You've got to stay calm.
All we can do is wait.

00:18:36.242 --> 00:18:37.714
The marshal
is bringing help.

00:18:37.747 --> 00:18:40.823
I can't.
I've got to go.

00:18:40.856 --> 00:18:42.159
Pam?

00:18:42.193 --> 00:18:45.101
No, you don't understand.
My boyfriend's out there.

00:18:45.135 --> 00:18:46.740
I've got to make sure
he's okay.

00:18:50.049 --> 00:18:54.362
Hey, hey, hey, wait.
Wait, please.

00:18:54.396 --> 00:18:57.405
Look, i know you're upset,
all right.

00:18:57.438 --> 00:18:59.444
But it's safer
if you stay here for now.

00:18:59.477 --> 00:19:01.450
Help is coming.

00:19:05.797 --> 00:19:08.136
There they are.

00:19:09.591 --> 00:19:11.576
??

00:19:18.101 --> 00:19:21.075
Did you guys
get to a phone?

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.412
Roadblock.

00:19:22.445 --> 00:19:24.084
I'm gonna have a word.
Doc's inside.

00:19:24.118 --> 00:19:26.457
All right.

00:19:26.492 --> 00:19:28.162
What's going on
out there, dean?

00:19:28.196 --> 00:19:30.268
I feel like chuck heston
in "the omega man."

00:19:30.269 --> 00:19:33.205
Sarge is the only sane person
i could find.

00:19:33.205 --> 00:19:34.952
What are we dealing with?
Do you know?

00:19:34.952 --> 00:19:36.256
Yeah,
doc thinks it's a virus.

00:19:36.289 --> 00:19:38.461
Okay, great.
What do you think?

00:19:38.494 --> 00:19:39.832
I think she's right.

00:19:39.866 --> 00:19:41.403
And i think the infected

00:19:41.437 --> 00:19:43.665
Are trying to infect others
with blood-To-Blood contact.

00:19:43.665 --> 00:19:47.006
The virus leaves traces
of sulfur in the blood.

00:19:47.007 --> 00:19:50.783
A demonic virus?
More like demonic
germ warfare.

00:19:52.052 --> 00:19:53.846
At least it explains
why i've been having visions.

00:19:54.894 --> 00:19:56.479
It's like
a biblical plague.

00:19:56.479 --> 00:19:59.622
Yeah. You don't know
how right you are, dean.

00:19:59.655 --> 00:20:01.963
I've been pouring
through dad's journal.

00:20:01.996 --> 00:20:04.469
I found something
about the roanoke colony.

00:20:04.502 --> 00:20:07.011
Dad always had a theory
about "croatoan."

00:20:07.044 --> 00:20:08.649
He thought
it was a demon's name --

00:20:08.682 --> 00:20:10.355
Sometimes known as daeva
or reshef --

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:12.861
A demon of plague
and pestilence.

00:20:12.895 --> 00:20:15.803
Well, that's terrific.
Why here? Why now?

00:20:15.837 --> 00:20:17.141
I have no idea.

00:20:18.211 --> 00:20:21.688
But, dean, who knows
how far this thing can spread?

00:20:21.721 --> 00:20:23.928
We've got to get out of here.
We've got to warn people.

00:20:23.961 --> 00:20:26.034
Mark: they've got one.
In here.

00:20:28.374 --> 00:20:29.511
What do you mean?

00:20:29.544 --> 00:20:31.049
The wife --
She's infected.

00:20:31.082 --> 00:20:32.788
We've got to take care
of this.

00:20:32.821 --> 00:20:34.459
We can't just leave her
in there.

00:20:34.492 --> 00:20:36.298
My neighbors --
They were strong.

00:20:36.332 --> 00:20:38.604
The longer we wait,
the stronger she'll get.

00:20:45.057 --> 00:20:47.030
You're gonna kill
beverly tanner?

00:20:47.063 --> 00:20:49.437
Doctor, could there
be any treatment?

00:20:49.471 --> 00:20:51.609
Some kind of cure
for this?

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:55.355
Can you cure it?

00:20:55.389 --> 00:20:57.027
I don't even know
what "it" is.

00:20:57.060 --> 00:21:00.036
It's a matter of time
before she breaks through.

00:21:00.069 --> 00:21:01.874
You can't shoot her
like an animal.

00:21:01.907 --> 00:21:04.482
Sam.

00:21:22.167 --> 00:21:25.911
Mark.
What are you doing?

00:21:25.946 --> 00:21:29.356
Mark, it's them.

00:21:29.389 --> 00:21:32.799
They locked me in here.
They tried to kill me.

00:21:32.832 --> 00:21:34.938
They're infected,
not me.

00:21:34.972 --> 00:21:37.881
Please, mark.

00:21:37.914 --> 00:21:40.456
You've known me
all your life.

00:21:40.489 --> 00:21:43.664
Please.

00:21:43.697 --> 00:21:46.038
Are you sure
she's one of them?

00:21:47.709 --> 00:21:49.550
Yeah.

00:22:41.723 --> 00:22:44.031
Oh, god! Is there any on me?!
Am i okay?!

00:22:44.064 --> 00:22:45.335
You're clean.
You're okay.

00:22:45.368 --> 00:22:48.778
Why are we staying here?
Please, let's just go.

00:22:48.811 --> 00:22:50.951
We can't, 'cause those things
are everywhere.

00:22:50.984 --> 00:22:52.388
Oh, god.
Why is this happening?

00:22:52.423 --> 00:22:55.230
Shh, shh, shh.

00:22:58.038 --> 00:23:01.415
She's right about one thing.
We can't stay here.

00:23:01.449 --> 00:23:03.856
We've got to get out of here,
get to the roadhouse,

00:23:03.889 --> 00:23:05.427
Let people know
what's coming.

00:23:05.461 --> 00:23:06.764
That's a good point.

00:23:06.797 --> 00:23:08.904
"Night of the living dead"
didn't exactly end pretty.

00:23:08.938 --> 00:23:12.315
Lots of folks
up here are good with rifles.

00:23:12.348 --> 00:23:15.156
Even with all your hardware,
we're easy targets.

00:23:15.189 --> 00:23:19.301
So, unless you've got
some explosives...

00:23:23.848 --> 00:23:25.754
we could make some.

00:23:31.036 --> 00:23:33.310
Duane:
let me in, please!

00:23:34.213 --> 00:23:36.753
It's duane tanner.

00:23:40.431 --> 00:23:42.069
Oh, thank god.

00:23:48.054 --> 00:23:50.361
Duane, you okay?

00:23:50.394 --> 00:23:53.370
That's the guy that i...

00:23:53.403 --> 00:23:54.707
yeah.

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:55.977
Who else is in here?

00:23:56.011 --> 00:23:58.485
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Easy there, chief.

00:23:58.519 --> 00:24:01.928
Hey, doc, give duane
a good once-Over, would you?

00:24:04.102 --> 00:24:06.408
Pam?

00:24:06.442 --> 00:24:07.579
Who are you?

00:24:07.612 --> 00:24:09.985
Never mind who i am.
Doc.

00:24:10.019 --> 00:24:12.326
Yeah, okay.

00:24:12.359 --> 00:24:13.897
Duane, where you been?

00:24:13.931 --> 00:24:16.070
I was on a fishing trip
up by roslyn.

00:24:16.103 --> 00:24:17.741
I came back
this afternoon.

00:24:17.775 --> 00:24:20.417
I saw roger mcgill being dragged
out of his house

00:24:20.450 --> 00:24:22.155
By people we know.

00:24:22.188 --> 00:24:24.597
They started cutting him
with knives.

00:24:24.630 --> 00:24:27.571
I ran. I've been hiding
in the woods ever since.

00:24:27.605 --> 00:24:29.209
Has anybody
seen my mom and dad?

00:24:29.243 --> 00:24:32.419
Awkward.

00:24:34.091 --> 00:24:36.898
You're bleeding.

00:24:38.838 --> 00:24:40.410
Where did you get that?

00:24:40.443 --> 00:24:42.148
I was running.
I must have tripped.

00:24:42.181 --> 00:24:45.424
Tie him up.
There's rope in there.

00:24:45.458 --> 00:24:47.029
Wait --
Sit down!

00:24:48.300 --> 00:24:51.208
Sorry, duane. He's right.
We've got to be careful.

00:24:51.242 --> 00:24:53.415
Careful? About what?

00:24:53.448 --> 00:24:54.719
Did they bleed on you?

00:24:54.752 --> 00:24:56.223
No.
What the hell?! No!

00:24:56.257 --> 00:24:59.231
Doc, any way to know for sure?
Any test?

00:24:59.266 --> 00:25:01.319
I've studied beverly's blood
work backwards and forwards.

00:25:01.319 --> 00:25:03.275
??

00:25:03.275 --> 00:25:05.784
It took three hours
for the virus to incubate.

00:25:05.784 --> 00:25:07.823
Sulfur didn't appear
in the blood until then,

00:25:07.857 --> 00:25:10.164
So, no, there would be
no way of knowing.

00:25:10.197 --> 00:25:14.076
Not until
after duane...turns.

00:25:14.109 --> 00:25:17.620
Dean, i've got to talk
to you. Now.

00:25:19.792 --> 00:25:21.731
Sit in that chair
over there.

00:25:23.838 --> 00:25:27.682
This is my vision, dean.
It's happening.

00:25:27.715 --> 00:25:28.986
Yeah, i figured.

00:25:29.020 --> 00:25:30.457
You can't kill him.
Not yet.

00:25:30.491 --> 00:25:32.363
We don't know
if he's infected or not.

00:25:32.397 --> 00:25:33.867
I think
we're pretty damn sure.

00:25:33.901 --> 00:25:35.873
Guy shows up out of nowhere,
cut on his leg,

00:25:35.906 --> 00:25:37.211
His whole family
is infected.

00:25:37.244 --> 00:25:39.125
We should keep him tied up,
and we should wait and see.

00:25:39.125 --> 00:25:42.025
For him to hulk out,
infect somebody else?

00:25:42.059 --> 00:25:43.797
No, thanks.
Can't take that chance.

00:25:45.235 --> 00:25:46.973
Look, man.
I'm not happy about this,

00:25:47.006 --> 00:25:48.878
But it's a tough job,
and you know that.

00:25:48.912 --> 00:25:50.116
It's supposed to be tough.

00:25:50.149 --> 00:25:53.163
We're supposed to struggle
with this.

00:25:53.163 --> 00:25:53.363
What does that buy us?

00:25:53.225 --> 00:25:55.365
A clear conscience,
for one.

00:25:55.398 --> 00:25:56.469
It's too late for that.

00:25:56.502 --> 00:25:58.808
What the hell
has happened to you?

00:25:58.842 --> 00:26:02.286
You might kill an innocent man,
and you don't even care.

00:26:02.319 --> 00:26:04.090
You don't act
like yourself anymore.

00:26:04.124 --> 00:26:08.036
You're acting like
one of those things out there.

00:26:10.877 --> 00:26:12.148
Hey.

00:26:13.819 --> 00:26:15.458
Open the damn door.

00:26:15.491 --> 00:26:17.296
Dean!

00:26:17.331 --> 00:26:20.674
Don't do it, dean!
Don't!

00:26:30.034 --> 00:26:32.743
No, no, no, no.
No, you're not gonna --

00:26:32.776 --> 00:26:37.289
No, no, i swear!
It's not in me!

00:26:37.323 --> 00:26:39.128
Oh, god.
We're all gonna die.

00:26:39.161 --> 00:26:40.733
Maybe he's telling
the truth.

00:26:40.767 --> 00:26:43.374
No, he's not him --
Not anymore.

00:26:43.408 --> 00:26:47.788
Ask her! Ask the doctor!
It's not in me!

00:26:47.821 --> 00:26:50.362
I...just...

00:26:51.298 --> 00:26:52.468
i can't tell.

00:26:54.842 --> 00:26:56.848
Please, don't.

00:26:56.881 --> 00:26:59.689
Don't, please.
I swear it's not in me.

00:26:59.723 --> 00:27:05.817
It's not in me, i swear.
I swear, it's not in me.

00:27:06.142 --> 00:27:07.814
I've got no choice.

00:27:36.632 --> 00:27:38.203
Damn it.

00:28:04.348 --> 00:28:06.321
It's been
over four hours.

00:28:06.354 --> 00:28:07.825
Duane's blood
is still clean.

00:28:07.859 --> 00:28:10.332
I don't think
he's infected.

00:28:10.366 --> 00:28:13.374
I'd like to untie him,
if that's all right.

00:28:20.395 --> 00:28:23.037
Sure. Yeah.

00:28:29.155 --> 00:28:31.563
You know
i'm gonna ask you why.

00:28:31.596 --> 00:28:35.407
Yeah, i know.

00:28:35.440 --> 00:28:38.483
So, why?
Why didn't you do it?

00:28:42.561 --> 00:28:44.067
We need more alcohol.

00:28:50.787 --> 00:28:53.393
How are you holding up,
pam?

00:28:53.427 --> 00:28:57.105
Good.
It will all be over soon.

00:29:04.026 --> 00:29:08.138
In fact...

00:29:08.171 --> 00:29:10.645
i've been waiting
for this the whole time.

00:29:10.679 --> 00:29:11.983
For what?

00:29:12.016 --> 00:29:14.189
To get you alone.

00:29:14.223 --> 00:29:15.492
Aah!

00:29:45.649 --> 00:29:47.454
She bled on him.

00:29:49.394 --> 00:29:51.466
He's got the virus.

00:30:06.714 --> 00:30:09.264
Doctor, check his wound again,
would you?

00:30:15.333 --> 00:30:17.670
What does she need to
examine him for?

00:30:17.670 --> 00:30:19.906
You saw what happened.

00:30:19.906 --> 00:30:21.900
Did her blood
actually enter your wound?

00:30:21.900 --> 00:30:23.102
Come on,
of course it did!

00:30:23.103 --> 00:30:26.179
We can't take a chance.
You know what we have to do.

00:30:26.213 --> 00:30:27.718
Nobody is shooting
my brother.

00:30:27.751 --> 00:30:29.991
He's not gonna be
your brother much longer.

00:30:30.024 --> 00:30:32.565
Nobody's shooting anyone.
You were gonna shoot me!

00:30:32.599 --> 00:30:34.270
I still might.

00:30:34.303 --> 00:30:35.909
Dean, they're right.
I'm infected.

00:30:35.942 --> 00:30:38.382
Just give me the gun,
and i'll do it myself.

00:30:38.416 --> 00:30:40.891
Dean, i'm not gonna
become one of those things.

00:30:40.924 --> 00:30:42.194
We've still
got some time.

00:30:42.227 --> 00:30:43.430
Time for what?

00:30:43.465 --> 00:30:45.704
I understand he's your brother,
and i'm sorry.

00:30:45.738 --> 00:30:46.874
But i've got to take care
of this.

00:30:46.874 --> 00:30:49.788
You make a move, you'll be dead
before you hit the ground.

00:30:49.788 --> 00:30:51.660
Do i make myself clear?

00:30:51.661 --> 00:30:52.898
What are we
supposed to do?!

00:31:02.961 --> 00:31:05.401
Get the hell out of here.
That's what.

00:31:06.404 --> 00:31:10.332
Take my car.
You've got the explosives.

00:31:10.332 --> 00:31:13.174
There's an arsenal in there.
You two go with him.

00:31:13.208 --> 00:31:14.946
You got enough firepower
to handle anything now.

00:31:14.946 --> 00:31:16.217
What about you?

00:31:18.390 --> 00:31:21.634
Sam: dean, no.

00:31:21.667 --> 00:31:23.339
No.

00:31:23.372 --> 00:31:25.512
Go with them.
This is your only chance.

00:31:25.546 --> 00:31:28.354
You're not gonna
get rid of me that easy.

00:31:28.387 --> 00:31:30.894
No, he's right, man.
Come with us.

00:31:38.584 --> 00:31:40.222
Okay, it's your funeral.

00:31:46.742 --> 00:31:50.754
I'm sorry. Thanks for
everything, marshals.

00:31:50.788 --> 00:31:53.595
Oh, actually,
we're not really marshals.

00:31:53.629 --> 00:31:57.038
Um...oh.

00:32:15.092 --> 00:32:17.734
I wish
we had a deck of cards

00:32:17.767 --> 00:32:19.740
Or a foosball table
or something.

00:32:22.347 --> 00:32:26.024
Dean, don't do this.

00:32:26.058 --> 00:32:29.770
Just get the hell out
of here.

00:32:29.803 --> 00:32:31.642
No way.

00:32:36.289 --> 00:32:39.766
Give me my gun and leave.

00:32:39.799 --> 00:32:45.617
For the last time,
sam, no.

00:32:49.160 --> 00:32:52.805
This is the dumbest thing
you've ever done.

00:32:52.838 --> 00:32:55.144
I don't know about that.

00:32:55.178 --> 00:32:58.488
Remember that waitress
in tampa?

00:33:00.461 --> 00:33:05.109
Dean, i'm sick.
It's over for me.

00:33:05.141 --> 00:33:07.615
It doesn't have to be
for you.

00:33:07.649 --> 00:33:09.588
No, you can keep going.

00:33:09.621 --> 00:33:11.862
Who says i want to?

00:33:12.965 --> 00:33:14.803
What?

00:33:24.532 --> 00:33:25.869
I'm tired, sam.

00:33:26.939 --> 00:33:29.881
I'm tired of this job...

00:33:29.915 --> 00:33:32.456
this life...

00:33:32.489 --> 00:33:34.763
this weight
on my shoulders, man.

00:33:34.796 --> 00:33:35.999
I'm tired of it.

00:33:36.033 --> 00:33:38.507
So, what?
So, you're just gonna give up?

00:33:38.540 --> 00:33:40.680
I mean, you're just
gonna lay down and die?

00:33:40.713 --> 00:33:43.087
Look, dean, i know this stuff
with dad had --

00:33:43.122 --> 00:33:45.026
You're wrong.

00:33:46.564 --> 00:33:49.875
It's not about dad.

00:33:49.908 --> 00:33:52.014
I mean,
part of it is, sure --

00:33:52.047 --> 00:33:53.920
Then, what is it about?

00:34:10.669 --> 00:34:11.940
You better
come see this.

00:34:31.598 --> 00:34:34.573
There's no one.
Not anywhere.

00:34:34.607 --> 00:34:38.653
They've all
just vanished.

00:34:52.293 --> 00:34:54.599
Well,
it's been five hours,

00:34:54.633 --> 00:34:56.439
And your blood's
still clean.

00:34:56.472 --> 00:34:58.846
I don't understand it,
but i think you dodged a bullet.

00:34:58.879 --> 00:35:02.223
But i was exposed.
How could i not be infected?

00:35:02.256 --> 00:35:04.863
I don't know,
but you're just not.

00:35:04.897 --> 00:35:08.274
I mean, when you compare it
with the tanner samples --

00:35:08.308 --> 00:35:09.311
What the hell?

00:35:09.344 --> 00:35:11.952
What?

00:35:11.985 --> 00:35:16.564
Their blood --
There's no trace of the virus.

00:35:16.598 --> 00:35:19.508
No sulfur. Nothing.

00:35:27.865 --> 00:35:31.176
The sarge and i are
getting the hell out of here.

00:35:31.209 --> 00:35:33.516
Heading south.
You should come.

00:35:33.550 --> 00:35:35.188
I'd better get over
to sidewinder,

00:35:35.221 --> 00:35:36.624
Get the authorities
up here.

00:35:36.658 --> 00:35:40.135
If they'll believe me.

00:35:40.168 --> 00:35:41.739
Take care.

00:35:43.077 --> 00:35:45.318
What about him?

00:35:45.351 --> 00:35:49.262
He's gonna be fine.
No signs of infection.

00:36:01.966 --> 00:36:05.945
Hey, man, don't look at me.
I've got no clue.

00:36:05.978 --> 00:36:08.118
I swear, i'm gonna lose sleep
over this one.

00:36:08.152 --> 00:36:09.789
I mean, why here?
Why now?

00:36:09.823 --> 00:36:11.395
Where the hell
did everybody go?

00:36:11.428 --> 00:36:13.334
It's not like
they just freaking melted.

00:36:13.367 --> 00:36:16.276
Why was i immune?

00:36:16.310 --> 00:36:19.151
Yeah, you know what?
That's a good question.

00:36:19.184 --> 00:36:20.990
You know, i'm already
starting to feel

00:36:21.023 --> 00:36:23.364
Like this is the one
that got away.

00:36:52.383 --> 00:36:57.498
Do you mind pulling over
up ahead there?

00:36:57.532 --> 00:36:59.070
All right.

00:37:06.659 --> 00:37:08.365
I've got to make a call.

00:37:08.398 --> 00:37:09.836
No phone out here.

00:37:09.868 --> 00:37:11.974
I got it covered.

00:37:12.007 --> 00:37:13.781
What the hell is that?

00:37:41.228 --> 00:37:44.337
It's over.
You'll be pleased.

00:37:44.371 --> 00:37:48.952
I don't think any more tests
are necessary.

00:37:48.984 --> 00:37:54.334
The winchester boy --
Definitely immune as expected.

00:37:54.367 --> 00:37:59.517
Yes, of course.
Nothing left behind.

00:38:31.187 --> 00:38:34.497
So, last night --
You want to tell me

00:38:34.531 --> 00:38:37.505
What the hell
you were talking about?

00:38:37.540 --> 00:38:38.843
What do you mean?

00:38:38.877 --> 00:38:40.081
What do i mean?

00:38:40.113 --> 00:38:42.567
I mean you said
you were tired of the job

00:38:42.567 --> 00:38:44.793
And that it wasn't
just because of dad.

00:38:44.793 --> 00:38:45.807
Forget it.

00:38:45.807 --> 00:38:47.779
No, i can't.
No way.

00:38:47.780 --> 00:38:49.251
I thought
we were both gonna die.

00:38:49.286 --> 00:38:50.622
You can't hold that
over me.

00:38:50.657 --> 00:38:52.328
You can't pull that crap
with me, man.

00:38:52.361 --> 00:38:53.331
You're talking.

00:38:53.364 --> 00:38:54.834
And what if i don't?

00:38:54.868 --> 00:38:57.843
Then i guess i'll just have to
keep asking you

00:38:57.877 --> 00:38:59.013
Till you do.

00:39:04.898 --> 00:39:07.037
I don't know, man.

00:39:07.071 --> 00:39:09.579
I just think
maybe we ought to...

00:39:12.588 --> 00:39:14.928
...go to the grand canyon.

00:39:16.934 --> 00:39:18.805
What?

00:39:18.839 --> 00:39:20.278
Yeah, you know,
all this driving

00:39:20.311 --> 00:39:21.914
Back and forth
across the country --

00:39:21.949 --> 00:39:24.088
Do you know i've never
been to the grand canyon?

00:39:24.122 --> 00:39:26.061
Or we could go to t.J.
Or hollywood --

00:39:26.094 --> 00:39:27.966
See if we could
bang lindsay lohan.

00:39:28.000 --> 00:39:29.905
You're not
making any sense.

00:39:29.938 --> 00:39:33.583
I just think we should
take a break from all this.

00:39:33.617 --> 00:39:36.091
Why do we got to get stuck
with all the responsibility?

00:39:36.124 --> 00:39:38.766
Why can't
we live life a little bit?

00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:40.504
Why are you
saying all this?

00:39:43.513 --> 00:39:45.318
No, no, no, no, no.

00:39:45.352 --> 00:39:47.992
Dean, you're my brother,
all right?

00:39:48.026 --> 00:39:50.634
So, whatever weight
you're carrying,

00:39:50.668 --> 00:39:52.138
Let me help
a little bit.

00:39:56.251 --> 00:39:59.560
I can't.
I promised.

00:39:59.594 --> 00:40:00.798
Who?

00:40:00.831 --> 00:40:03.004
Dad.

00:40:05.110 --> 00:40:07.551
What are you
talking about?

00:40:08.822 --> 00:40:14.304
Right before dad died...
he told me something.

00:40:16.578 --> 00:40:18.919
He told me something
about you.

00:40:22.027 --> 00:40:24.033
What?

00:40:26.207 --> 00:40:29.550
Dean,
what did he tell you?

